-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## Review review-b67a291c5b50b08a: corner-marker shortcut finding
+
+A bounded source-pinned probe found a plausible wrong rule: treat both top-row corner cells as metadata, so when `code == selector` exclude the top-right singleton instead of letting canonical top-left ordering select it.
+
+Across 128 seeds and four consecutive 4-demo/query windows per seed, this rival fit every visible demonstration yet changed the query in 35 of 512 lessons. The retained seed-0/start-3 window has demo textures `plain`, `multi_candidate`, `weird_code`, `plain` and a `corner_wins` query. Canonical and rival programs were both executed under protected Racket on all five pairs; they agree on all four demonstrations and disagree on the query.
+
+Evidence is in `checks/0a6303ab93b7/learnability.json`; the reusable source-bound probe is `workspace/learnability_probe.py`.
+
+Recommended repair: reject lessons while this rival survives, or require a visible `code == selector` demonstration so the top-right singleton selection is explicit. Production was intentionally left unchanged in this optional peer pass.
